            <ArticleTitle>Intestinal lymphangiectasia without protein loss in a child with abdominal pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>246-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 7-year-old white girl presented with recurrent abdominal pain because of gastroesophageal reflux. At endoscopy, we found intestinal lymphangiectasia in the duodenal biopsy. There were no physical signs, nor any laboratory evidence of enteric protein loss.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
